From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] icacls, cacls: display and change the access control lists of files (3520)

icacls, cacls: display and change the access control lists of files

icacls shows a file's DACL in the documented layout (trustee, inheritance flags, rights), and does
/grant, /grant:r, /deny, /remove[:g|:d], /reset, /setowner, /inheritance:e|d|r, /findsid, /save, /T, /C,
/Q, /L, with the "Successfully processed n files; Failed processing n files" summary and exit codes.
cacls does /E, /G, /P, /R, /D, /T, /C on the same calls. Both go through GetNamedSecurityInfo and
SetNamedSecurityInfo, so what a person may change is the system's decision.
---
--- a/programs/icacls/icacls_main.c
+++ b/programs/icacls/icacls_main.c
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
